---
tone:
  - { where: "Welcome screen", mood: "Warm and encouraging", at: 12, copy: "Welcome to Fettle, Sam. Find a class you'll enjoy and book it in 2 taps." }
  - { where: "Class booked", mood: "Warm, with the facts", at: 25, copy: "You're booked on Spin, Thursday 6:30pm. See you there." }
  - { where: "Class full", mood: "Helpful, a bit more matter-of-fact", at: 45, copy: "Spin is full. Join the waiting list and we'll text you if a place comes up." }
  - { where: "Something went wrong", mood: "Calm and practical", at: 60, copy: "We couldn't load your bookings. Check your connection and try again." }
  - { where: "Payment failed", mood: "Serious and clear about what happens", at: 78, copy: "Your payment didn't go through, so your membership hasn't renewed. Update your card by 30 November to keep booking." }
  - { where: "Deleting an account", mood: "Serious, careful, no persuasion", at: 92, copy: "Deleting your account removes all your bookings and history. This cannot be undone." }
rules:
  - { title: "Dates", rule: "Day, date and month. Short form in tight spaces. No ordinals or slashes.", do: "Thursday 14 November · Thu 14 Nov", dont: "14/11 · 14th Nov · 11-14" }
  - { title: "Times", rule: "12-hour clock, with am or pm and no space. Use “midday” and “midnight”.", do: "6:30pm · midday", dont: "18:30 · 6.30 PM · 12pm" }
  - { title: "Numbers", rule: "Numerals for every number, so they stand out when people scan.", do: "3 places left · £45 a month", dont: "three spaces remaining · £45.00/mo" }
  - { title: "Capital letters", rule: "Sentence case everywhere, including buttons and headings. Class names are proper nouns.", do: "Book class · Yoga Flow", dont: "Book A Class · JOIN CLASS" }
  - { title: "Contractions", rule: "Use them, so the app sounds like a person. Write “cannot” in full only in serious warnings.", do: "You're booked · We'll text you", dont: "You are now booked · We will text you" }
  - { title: "Exclamation marks", rule: "At most one, and only for real celebrations. Never in errors or anything about money.", do: "Your first class is booked!", dont: "Oops! Payment failed!" }
  - { title: "Emoji", rule: "None in interface text. Screen readers read them out, so 💪 becomes “flexed biceps”.", do: "You're booked on Spin", dont: "You're booked 💪🔥" }
  - { title: "Inclusive language", rule: "Describe classes by what happens, not who they're for or how bodies should look.", do: "Low-impact strength · All levels", dont: "Ladies' toning · Get bikini ready" }
  - { title: "Words to avoid", rule: "No hype, no shame, and no words that make exercise sound easy for everyone.", do: "Book · Waiting list · Try", dont: "Crush it · Beast mode · Burn off that pizza · Simply · Easy" }
---
